# The scripts here carry a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang and are run on Linux
# and macOS. A checkout on Windows applies core.autocrlf and rewrites every text
# file to CRLF, after which the shebang reads as `bash\r` and executing one
# fails with
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which names the interpreter rather than the script, and so reads as though the
# script itself were missing.
#
# The oracle trees are the other reason. A golden is compared byte for byte
# against what the binary writes, and a line ending rewritten on checkout fails
# every one of them for a reason no diff explains.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
